FAIL	wardroper-sick-nursing-1892	https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2421674/fullTextXML	HTTP 404 — no XML full text. Europe PMC search AUTH:"Nightingale F" returns this as "The Reform of Sick Nursing and the late Mrs. Wardroper", BMJ 1892, i.e. a signed contribution by her to the BMJ. Europe PMC holds it as a scanned PDF only, so no machine-readable text could be obtained. THIS IS THE MOST REGRETTABLE LOSS IN THE BATCH: it is a signed periodical article by her that no other source in this corpus duplicates.
FAIL	manuscript-notes-bmj-1920	https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2337637/fullTextXML	HTTP 404 — no XML full text. "Some Manuscript Notes by Florence Nightingale", BMJ 1920 Jun 12;1(3102):798-799 — prints previously unpublished notes in her own hand. Scanned-PDF-only on Europe PMC.
FAIL	obit-bmj-1910	https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2335760/fullTextXML	HTTP 404 — no XML full text. Her principal British obituary, BMJ 1910 Aug 20;2(2590):437-439. Scanned-PDF-only. Partly compensated: the Glasgow Medical Journal and Buffalo Medical Journal obituaries of the same weeks WERE obtained (obit-glasgow-1910, obit-buffalo-1910).
FAIL	obit-california-1910	https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1893331/fullTextXML	HTTP 404 — no XML full text. California State Journal of Medicine 1910;8(10):337. Scanned-PDF-only.
#
#   PATTERN: all four failures are the same failure. Europe PMC's `isOpenAccess` flag was
#   "N" for each of them, and for pre-1923 scanned material an "N" means the article exists
#   only as page images. No amount of retrying changes this; a different route (OCR of the
#   PDF) was not attempted because it would have produced text of unknown fidelity that
#   could not be distinguished downstream from a clean transcription.
#
